: "212196453", "author": {"steamid": "76561197988362667", "personaname": "Tibbles", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197988362667/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 46179, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1377, "playtime_at_review": 34825, "last_played": 1787886579, "avatar": "c074df990c009dbaddd475bc45b906325a29e8a4"}, "language": "english", "review": "One adrenaline pumping, action packed, enjoyable but buggy mess of a game. Still worth playing. Over the top non-stop action and combat. Absolutely the best way to act and play guilt free as a trigger happy human supremacist in a cog of a dystopian totalitarian regime in a false utopia besieged and surrounded by enemies  (That's not in a WH40K universe).\n\nThe worst part about this game is the constant game balance issue between patches and the random game crashes and in game bugs that are constantly introduced, fixed, then reintroduces after each patch. It's PVE and you get a good ironic laugh when you bleed and sweat for the objectives just to have it bugged out or crash just before completion. It doesn't happen often, but it makes you think to yourself; are you a masochist or a patriot, or maybe both. You'll rage because your sacrifice for democracy was in vain as it won't be recognize by anyone but those who helldived with you. Super Earth will give you the weapons and tools you need, not the ones you want, and they will take it away just as quick.  Yet in the end, you'll dive again and again with other fellow Helldivers.", "timestamp_created": 1764546990, "timestamp_updated": 1764549172, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1707382200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "212195495", "author": {"steamid": "76561198